---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Deluge Tools — open source utilities for the Synthstrom Deluge.">
  <section class="about">
    <h1 class="about-title">About</h1>
    <p>Deluge Tools is an open-source project for the <a href="https://synthstrom.com/product/deluge/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Synthstrom Deluge</a> community.</p>
    <p>The Deluge stores songs as XML files on an SD card. These tools parse that format and convert it into standard music formats — so you can see your arrangements as sheet music, inspect song structure, or import MIDI compositions.</p>
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>Everything runs in your browser. The Python conversion library is compiled to WebAssembly via <a href="https://pyodide.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pyodide</a>, so your files never leave your machine. No server, no account, no upload.</p>
    <h2>Source</h2>
    <p>The code is on GitHub. Contributions welcome — especially from the Deluge community.</p>
    <h2>Built with</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Astro</a> + <a href="https://svelte.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Svelte</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://pyodide.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Pyodide</a> (Python in WebAssembly)</li>
      <li>Hosted on <a href="https://vercel.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vercel</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    max-width: 600px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 5rem;
  }
  .about-title {
    font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .about h2 {
    font-family: 'DM Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .about p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .about ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .about li {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    padding: 0.25rem 0;
  }
  .about li::before {
    content: "→ ";
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
